msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/maintain-docs.rst:40
msgid "``guidedog gds`` runs the commands of ``dsc`` on this catalog; see :doc:`discussions`. It manages metadata, numbers, state, and recovery. Its RST publication path calls the project engine. It produces a complete HTML site and a separate PDF for each record. A selector limits the PDFs. HTML remains a coherent site with a complete catalog. A selected PDF preview uses ``_build/selected/<artifact>/pdf``. It leaves the complete catalog in ``_build/pdf`` intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/maintain-docs.rst:54
msgid "The ordinary project commands work too. The GDS project uses its own ``conf.toml`` and its own ``_build`` directory. Read ``docs/gds/workflow.rst`` for the authoring workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/maintain-docs.rst:58
msgid "Before publishing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/maintain-docs.rst:61
msgid "Check links and diagnostics. Inspect wide tables and code blocks. Render the PDF pages after changing typography. Test the HTML at desktop and phone widths, in light and dark modes. Make sure the mathematics and diagrams work without a network connection. For engine changes, run the relevant library and integration tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:1
msgid "Move a Sphinx project to Guidedog"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:4
msgid "Guidedog is designed with Sphinx compatibility in mind. It uses the familiar directory structure, understands standard reStructuredText and MyST Markdown markup, recognizes the same configuration setting names, and implements Sphinx's Jinja template variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:8
msgid "However, there is an essential architectural difference: Sphinx executes arbitrary Python code in ``conf.py`` and relies on a Python virtual environment with external packages. Guidedog, by contrast, operates as a standalone compiled executable that reads pure data from ``conf.toml``. It does not execute Python scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:13
msgid "Migrating a project therefore centers on separating declarative configuration data from executable Python logic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:16
msgid "Migration workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:19
msgid "The migration process follows a structured sequence:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:23
msgid "conf.py is converted by guidedog migrate into conf.toml, followed by semantic verification, custom object mapping, and visual inspection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:23
msgid "The step-by-step workflow for migrating a Sphinx project to Guidedog."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:42
msgid "Step 1: Automated configuration migration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:45
msgid "Guidedog provides an automated migration tool that parses your existing ``conf.py``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:51
msgid "What ``guidedog migrate`` does:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:53
msgid "It extracts literal configuration values (strings, numbers, booleans, lists, and tables) and converts them to standard TOML syntax in ``conf.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:55
msgid "It detects standard Sphinx settings (such as ``project``, ``author``, ``extensions``, ``templates_path``, ``html_theme``, ``intersphinx_mapping``, and ``html_context``) and maps them cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:58
msgid "It identifies dynamically computed expressions (such as Python calls like ``version = get_version()`` or ``git_revision = subprocess.check_output(...)``). Because Guidedog does not execute Python, it flags these computed values in its migration report so you can provide explicit, static values in ``conf.toml``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:63
msgid "Review the generated ``conf.toml`` and replace any flagged expressions with static values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:65
msgid "Step 2: The three-pass verification strategy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:68
msgid "Once ``conf.toml`` is created, work through the migration in three focused passes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:70
msgid "Pass 1: Verify the document graph"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:73
msgid "Check that Guidedog discovers all documents and builds the expected hierarchy:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:75
msgid "Verify that ``root_doc`` points to your primary entry point (usually ``index`` or ``contents``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:76
msgid "Confirm that ``source_suffix`` lists all extensions you use (for example, ``[\".rst\", \".md\"]``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:77
msgid "Check ``exclude_patterns`` to ensure build folders, virtual environments, and temporary files are excluded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:79
msgid "Run a quick semantic check using the dummy builder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:85
msgid "The dummy builder checks every document and link without writing HTML files. Address any warnings about missing documents or malformed file includes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:88
msgid "Pass 2: Verify references, domains, and custom objects"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:91
msgid "Next, verify that cross-references and domain directives resolve:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:93
msgid "**Standard domains:** Guidedog natively supports the standard Python, C, C++, and JavaScript domains, along with standard role syntax like ``:py:func:``, ``:c:type:``, and ``:cpp:class:``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:95
msgid "**Intersphinx links:** If your Sphinx project linked to external documentation via Intersphinx, keep your ``[intersphinx_mapping]`` in ``conf.toml``. Guidedog fetches and parses standard ``objects.inv`` files natively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:98
msgid "**Declarative custom object types:** In Sphinx, projects often wrote small Python extensions calling ``app.add_object_type()`` to create custom directives and roles (such as ``.. confval::`` or ``.. setting::``). In Guidedog, you define these declaratively in ``conf.toml`` under ``[[object_types]]`` without writing any code. See :doc:`../object-types`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:103
msgid "Pass 3: Verify presentation and templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:106
msgid "Finally, verify the rendered visual appearance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:108
msgid "**HTML website:** Run ``guidedog build html path/to/docs -W`` and inspect the generated pages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:109
msgid "**Jinja templates:** Guidedog's native Jinja engine supports block inheritance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/migrate.rst:118
msgid "**PDF books:** Build a PDF book with ``guidedog build pdf path/to/docs -W``. Guidedog typesets the book using Typst and ``_templates/book.typ``, providing instant vector math, proper hyphenation, and running headers without requiring a LaTeX installation."
msgstr ""

