#: ../../howto/publish.rst:1
msgid "Build and publish documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:4
msgid "Publishing documentation involves turning raw reStructuredText and Markdown sources into static artifacts, verifying their integrity, and deploying them to a hosting environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:8
msgid "Guidedog separates the process of building a site from the process of deploying it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:10
msgid "**Building:** Guidedog reads your sources, compiles templates, resolves cross-references, and outputs a complete, verified directory of static HTML files or a typeset PDF book."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:12
msgid "**Publishing:** The resulting static files are served by your web server or deployed to a hosting destination, such as GitHub Pages, an S3 bucket, or an internal file server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:15
msgid "Because the output consists entirely of standard static files (HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and SVG), it can be served by any static web server (such as Nginx, Apache, or Caddy) without requiring an Odin runtime, Python interpreter, or active server process in production."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:19
msgid "Atomic publication architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:22
msgid "A critical design requirement is to publish complete output generations. The host finishes preparation before deciding a journaled commit. A failed preparation leaves the previous site intact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:26
msgid "Guidedog prepares a complete generation before deciding a journaled commit:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:30
msgid "A complete staged generation is journaled and switched into place. Recovery finishes or restores an interrupted commit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:30
msgid "The atomic staging and generation switch process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:48
msgid "How atomic commits protect your site:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:50
msgid "**Staging:** All newly rendered pages are written to a hidden staging folder beside the destination (``.<target>.next``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:52
msgid "**Isolation:** The existing live output directory is untouched while pages are being compiled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:53
msgid "**Failure safety:** If any page fails to render or if warnings-as-errors (``-W``) is triggered, the staging folder is abandoned. The existing live site remains completely unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:55
msgid "**Atomic swap:** Once all files are flushed, Guidedog switches the staging directory into place. On supported filesystems, this is an instantaneous directory exchange."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:57
msgid "**Interrupted recovery:** If a crash occurs during the swap, the durable journal ensures that the subsequent build settles the interrupted commit rather than guessing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:60
msgid "Standard build workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:63
msgid "To build both HTML and PDF outputs into the default project output directory:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:70
msgid "Output locations:"
