#: ../../howto/publish.rst:72
msgid "The HTML website is written to ``docs/manual/_build/html/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:73
msgid "The PDF book is written to ``docs/manual/_build/pdf/``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:75
msgid "The ``-j auto`` flag parallelizes document parsing across all available CPU cores."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:77
msgid "Custom output directories"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:80
msgid "To direct the compiled website to an explicit target folder (for example, in a CI/CD pipeline or deployment script), use the Sphinx-compatible command form:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:87
msgid "Guidedog enforces safety constraints on output paths:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:89
msgid "Choose a dedicated output folder, such as ``_build/html`` inside the project or ``build/site`` beside it. The output must not be the source root or one of its ancestors, because switching it would replace the source project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:92
msgid "When targeting a custom destination such as ``build/site``, Guidedog places internal caches in a sibling directory (such as ``build/.site.guidedog/.doctrees``), ensuring that the published folder contains only clean, deployable static assets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:96
msgid "Semantic checks and pre-flight validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:99
msgid "To verify the semantic validity of a project without writing HTML files to disk, use the ``dummy`` builder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:106
msgid "The dummy builder:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:108
msgid "Reads all documents and executes all syntax parsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:109
msgid "Resolves all toctrees, headings, cross-references, and domain objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:110
msgid "Checks document references and domain objects (``-n`` enables nitpicky cross-reference checking). It does not make HTTP requests to test external URLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:112
msgid "Exits with status 1 if any broken link or warning is found (``-W``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:114
msgid "Use the dummy builder in continuous integration pipelines for fast validation before running the full site rendering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:117
msgid "Reproducible build timestamps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:120
msgid "Documentation builds often embed timestamps (for example, in \"Last updated\" footer notices). For automated deployments where you want byte-for-byte reproducible outputs across multiple runs, pin the clock using the standard ``SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`` environment variable:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:128
msgid "When this variable is set, Guidedog uses the specified Unix epoch timestamp instead of the current system clock for all date formatting and template variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:131
msgid "Deployment options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:134
msgid "Once the build succeeds, deploy the static files to your hosting infrastructure:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:136
msgid "**Static web servers (Nginx / Caddy / Apache):** Point the server's root directive directly to the built HTML directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:138
msgid "**Cloud storage buckets (AWS S3 / Cloudflare R2 / Google Cloud Storage):** Sync the contents of ``_build/html`` to your bucket using your cloud provider's CLI tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:140
msgid "**GitHub Pages:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:142
msgid "For automated CI/CD deployments using GitHub Actions, see :doc:`github-pages`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:143
msgid "For direct deployments from your local machine, use ``guidedog-pages`` or a custom publisher plugin as described in :doc:`../plugins`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../howto/publish.rst:146
msgid "On filesystems with directory exchange, the output path switches in one operation. The fallback uses two renames and can briefly leave that path absent. It still never exposes a partly assembled tree. Journal recovery finishes or restores an interrupted switch. A client making several requests can span two generations; the build does not promise a snapshot for an entire browsing session."
msgstr ""
